Use case: stylized-concept. Asset type: one original seamless grayscale bark albedo tile for Cinder's pixelated 2.5D Living Forest. Primary request: create a square 1024x1024 flat material texture, filling the entire image edge to edge, of dense sinewy organic bark from immense alien trunks. Broad irregular vertical folded ridges, deep black fissures, layered fibrous skin, occasional small concentric wood knots; enough large structure to read on a 30-pixel-wide trunk. Style: hand-painted low-resolution game texture with deliberate hard-edged clustered pixels and restrained dithering, not smooth photographic noise. Color palette: grayscale only, charcoal grooves through pale gray raised sinews; the runtime will tint it scarlet/violet. Composition: orthographic flat surface without perspective, complete continuous texture, seamless left/right and top/bottom, no vignette, no directional spotlight, no border. Avoid: trees as objects, ground, scene, characters, faces, eyes, mouths, text, symbols, captions, watermark, transparent background, three-dimensional mockup, UI, whole concept painting. No new gameplay cue.
